# Rust Documentation

Use `///` for items, `//!` for modules. First line = brief summary.

**Sections:** `# Arguments`, `# Returns` (when relevant), `# Example` / `# Examples`, `# Panics`, `# Errors` (for `Result`), `# Safety` (for `unsafe`).

**Error variants:** Document what causes each, how to fix, and an example if useful.

```rust
// ✅ GOOD
/// Returns the variable name including any type suffix (e.g., "count%").
fn name(&self) -> &str

// ❌ BAD
/// Returns the name.
fn name(&self) -> &str
```

Use rustdoc link syntax `` [`Type::method`] `` for related items. Document the "why" when non-obvious. Run `cargo doc --no-deps` and `cargo test --doc` to verify.
